مُحَمَّدٌ بَشَرٌ لَا كَالبَشَرْ / بَلْ هُوَ يَاقُوتٌ بَيْنَ الحَجَرْ
Muḥammadun basharun lā ka-l-bashar / bal huwa yāqūtun bayna l-ḥajar
Muhammad is a man, but not like other men — rather he is a ruby among ordinary stones.

مُحَمَّدٌ مِفْتَاحُهُ بِسْمِ اللهِ / وَيَحْمَدُ اللهَ مَعَ الخَبَرْ
Muḥammadun miftāḥuhu bismi llāhi / wa yaḥmadu llāha maʿa l-khabar
Muhammad — his opening key is Bismillāh, and he praises God along with the tidings he brings.

مُحَمَّدٌ رَسُولٌ لِرَبِّ العُلَى / لِكَافَّةِ الخَلْقِ بِلَا نُكُرْ
Muḥammadun rasūlun li-rabbi l-ʿulā / li-kāffati l-khalqi bi-lā nukur
Muhammad is the Messenger of the Lord of the heights, sent to all creation without exception.

مُحَمَّدٌ بَعْثُهُ عَامَّةً / عَلَى العَالَمِينَ حَتَّى الشَّجَرْ
Muḥammadun baʿthuhu ʿāmmatan / ʿala l-ʿālamīna ḥatta sh-shajar
Muhammad's mission is universal, over all the worlds — even the trees.

مُحَمَّدٌ مَوْلِدُهُ مَكَّةُ / وَهِجْرَتُهُ طَيْبَةُ الغُرَرْ
Muḥammadun mawliduhu makkatu / wa hijratuhu ṭaybatu l-ghurar
Muhammad — his birthplace is Makkah, and his emigration was to radiant Ṭaybah.

مُحَمَّدٌ أَسْرَى مِنْ حَرَمٍ / إِلَى الأَيْلِيَاءِ مَأْوَى الحَرَرْ
Muḥammadun asrā min ḥaramin / ila l-ayliyāʾi maʾwa l-ḥarar
Muhammad journeyed by night from the Sanctuary to Īliyāʾ, refuge of the noble and free.

مُحَمَّدٌ مِعْرَاجُهُ ثَابِتٌ / بِنَصِّ الحَدِيثِ مَعَ العِبَرْ
Muḥammadun miʿrājuhu thābitun / bi-naṣṣi l-ḥadīthi maʿa l-ʿibar
Muhammad's ascension is firmly established by the text of ḥadīth, along with its lessons.

مُحَمَّدٌ فَاقَ جَمِيعَ الوَرَى / حَتَّى المُرْسَلِينَ ذَوِي الفَخَرْ
Muḥammadun fāqa jamīʿa l-warā / ḥatta l-mursalīna dhawi l-fakhar
Muhammad surpassed all creation — even the messengers, possessors of glory.

مُحَمَّدٌ مِنْ آدَمَ دُونَهُ / وَمَنْ بَعْدَهُ فَاعْجَبْ لِلْخَبَرْ
Muḥammadun min ādama dūnahu / wa man baʿdahu fa-ʿjab li-l-khabar
Muhammad — from Adam onward, all are beneath him, and all who came after: marvel at this report.

مُحَمَّدٌ أُمَّتُهُ خِيَرَةٌ / لِكُلِّ القُرُونِ مَعَ الزُّمَرْ
Muḥammadun ummatuhu khiyaratun / li-kulli l-qurūni maʿa z-zumar
Muhammad — his community is the chosen best of all ages and all throngs.

فَمِنْهُمْ شُمُوسٌ كَأَصْحَابِهِ / وَكَالغَوْثِ الجِيلِيِّ عَبْدِ القَادِرْ
Fa-minhum shumūsun ka-aṣḥābihi / wa ka-l-ghawthi l-jīliyyi ʿabdi l-qādir
Among them are suns like his Companions, and like the Ghawth al-Jīlī, ʿAbd al-Qādir.

مُحَمَّدٌ عِصْمَتُهُ مُحَتَّمٌ / صَغِيرًا كَبِيرًا بِلَا نُكُرْ
Muḥammadun ʿiṣmatuhu muḥattamun / ṣaghīran kabīran bi-lā nukur
Muhammad's protection from sin is certain, in youth and in age, beyond all denial.

مُحَمَّدٌ مَحَبَّتُهُ وَاجِبٌ / مِنَ المُؤْمِنِينَ عَلَى البَشَرْ
Muḥammadun maḥabbatuhu wājibun / mina l-muʾminīna ʿala l-bashar
Muhammad — love of him is an obligation binding on the believers among mankind.

مُحَمَّدٌ بَاغِضُهُ كَافِرٌ / يُعَذَّبُ دَوْمًا عَلَى الجَمَرْ
Muḥammadun bāghiḍuhu kāfirun / yuʿadhdhabu dawman ʿala l-jamar
Muhammad — whoever hates him is a disbeliever, punished forever upon the embers.

مُحَمَّدٌ قَاسِمٌ خَيْرُ المَلَا / وَمُعْطِي الحَقِيقَةِ ذُو الكِبَرْ
Muḥammadun qāsimun khayru l-malā / wa muʿṭi l-ḥaqīqati dhu l-kibar
Muhammad is the distributor, the best of the assembly — while the true Giver is the One of Greatness.

مُحَمَّدٌ وَاصِفُهُ رَبُّهُ / فَمَا لِضَعِيفٍ مِنَ الغُمَرْ
Muḥammadun wāṣifuhu rabbuhu / fa-mā li-ḍaʿīfin mina l-ghumar
Muhammad — his describer is his own Lord; so what has a weak nobody of the common crowd to add?

مِقْدَارُ مَا مِثْلُ ذَرٍّ ... / صِفَةُ عَرْشِ رَبِّي أَعْلَى الكِبَرْ
Miqdāru mā mithlu dharrin … / ṣifatu ʿarshi rabbī aʿla l-kibar
Whatever measure I could give is like a mote beside the description of my Lord's Throne, highest in greatness.

مُحَمَّدٌ رَأَى رَبَّهُ جَهْرَةً / بِيَقْظَةٍ مَعَ جِسْمِهِ الأَنْوَرْ
Muḥammadun raʾā rabbahu jahratan / bi-yaqẓatin maʿa jismihi l-anwar
Muhammad saw his Lord openly, while awake, together with his luminous body.

مُحَمَّدٌ يَجْزِي إِلَهُ الوَرَى / لِعَبْدٍ صَلَّى مَرَّةً عَشَرْ
Muḥammadun yajzī ilāhu l-warā / li-ʿabdin ṣallā marratan ʿashar
Muhammad — the God of creation rewards the servant who sends blessings once with tenfold.

كَعَبْدٍ صَلَّى عَشَرَةً مِائَةً / إِلَى أَلْفِ أَلْفٍ مَعَ الحُرَرْ
Ka-ʿabdin ṣallā ʿasharatan miʾatan / ilā alfi alfin maʿa l-ḥurar
And the servant who sends ten receives a hundred — on up to a thousand thousand, together with noble gifts.

وَمَنْ حَبَّهُ نَالَ مَا رَامَهُ / وَبُحْبُوحَ فِرْدَوْسٍ كَالدُّرَرْ
Wa man ḥabbahu nāla mā rāmahu / wa buḥbūḥa firdawsin ka-d-durar
Whoever loves him attains what he sought, and the very heart of Firdaws, gleaming like pearls.

اللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى الهَاشِمِيِّ / بِأَلْفِ أُلُوفٍ بِلَا حَصَرْ
Allāhumma ṣalli ʿala l-hāshimiyy / bi-alfi ulūfin bi-lā ḥaṣar
O God, bless the Hāshimī — by a thousand thousands, beyond all counting.

اللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى المُصْطَفَى / بِعَدِّ النُّجُومِ مَعَ الشَّجَرْ
Allāhumma ṣalli ʿala l-muṣṭafā / bi-ʿaddi n-nujūmi maʿa sh-shajar
O God, bless the Chosen One — by the number of the stars and the trees.

اللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى الكَامِلِ / بِعَدِّ النِّسَاءِ مَعَ الذَّكَرْ
Allāhumma ṣalli ʿala l-kāmil / bi-ʿaddi n-nisāʾi maʿa dh-dhakar
O God, bless the Perfect One — by the number of all women and men.

اللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى الأَنْوَرِ / بِعَدِّ رِضَاكَ مَعَ القَدَرْ
Allāhumma ṣalli ʿala l-anwar / bi-ʿaddi riḍāka maʿa l-qadar
O God, bless the Most Radiant — by the measure of Your good pleasure and Your decree.

اللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى الأَمْجَدِ / بِعَدِّ الحَصَاةِ مَعَ المَدَرْ
Allāhumma ṣalli ʿala l-amjad / bi-ʿaddi l-ḥaṣāti maʿa l-madar
O God, bless the Most Glorious — by the number of the pebbles and the clods of earth.

اللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى العَاقِبِ / بِعَدِّ مَعْلُومَاتِكَ الغُرَرْ
Allāhumma ṣalli ʿala l-ʿāqib / bi-ʿaddi maʿlūmātika l-ghurar
O God, bless the Last-Coming One — by the number of all the shining things You know.

اللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى الحَاشِرِ / بِأَنْفَاسِ خَلْقِكَ مَعَ نَظَرْ
Allāhumma ṣalli ʿala l-ḥāshir / bi-anfāsi khalqika maʿa naẓar
O God, bless the Gatherer — by the breaths of Your creation and every glance of their eyes.

اللَّهُمَّ [صَلِّ] عَلَى الشَّافِعِ / بِعَدِّ العُصَاةِ مَعَ البَرَرْ
Allāhumma [ṣalli] ʿala sh-shāfiʿ / bi-ʿaddi l-ʿuṣāti maʿa l-barar
O God, bless the Intercessor — by the number of the sinful and the righteous alike.

اللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى الخَاتِمِ / بِعَدِّ مَلَائِكَةٍ الغُرَرْ
Allāhumma ṣalli ʿala l-khātim / bi-ʿaddi malāʾikatin l-ghurar
O God, bless the Seal — by the number of the resplendent angels.

وَسَلِّمْ بِأَضْعَافِ مَا قَدْ مَضَى / مَتَى حُبُّهُ ضَاءَ كَالقَمَرْ
Wa sallim bi-aḍʿāfi mā qad maḍā / matā ḥubbuhu ḍāʾa ka-l-qamar
And grant peace many times over all that has passed, so long as love of him shines like the moon.

وَآلٍ وَصَحْبٍ وَأَتْبَاعِهِ / إِلَى يَوْمِ يُحْشَرُ لِلْبَشَرْ
Wa ālin wa ṣaḥbin wa atbāʿihi / ilā yawmi yuḥsharu li-l-bashar
And upon his family, his companions, and his followers, until the Day when mankind is gathered.

وَارْضَ عَنْ أَبِي بَكْرٍ مَعَ عُمَرْ / وَعُثْمَانَ مَعَ عَلِيٍّ المُضَرْ
Wa-rḍa ʿan abī bakrin maʿa ʿumar / wa ʿuthmāna maʿa ʿaliyyin il-muḍar
And be pleased with Abū Bakr and ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān and ʿAlī of Muḍar.

وَارْحَمْ يَا إِلَهِي لِنَاظِمِهَا / كَذَا المُنْشِدِينَ مَعَ الحُضَرْ
Wa-rḥam yā ilāhī li-nāẓimihā / kadha l-munshidīna maʿa l-ḥuḍar
And have mercy, O my God, on the one who composed it, likewise on those who chant it and those present.